=product @PRODUCER@ @BASE@ FLEX @PCSIVERSION@ full
1 'PRODUCER
=prompt @PRODUCER@
1 'PRODUCT
=prompt flex @VERSION@ for OpenVMS
1 'NOTICE
=prompt flex is free software under a BSD-style licence (see COPYING).
1 RELEASE_NOTES
=prompt Documentation is in [FLEX.DOC]README.VMS under the installation directory.
1 POST_INSTALL
=prompt Post-installation tasks for flex
    At system startup: to define FLEX$ROOT at every boot, add this line to
    SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM (after the line for M4$STARTUP.COM):
    $ @SYS$STARTUP:FLEX$STARTUP.COM
    For each user: to define the flex command, add this line to LOGIN.COM:
    $ @FLEX$ROOT:[000000]FLEX$SETUP.COM

PRODUCT REMOVE FLEX removes the product and deassigns FLEX$ROOT.
